<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Github.com on knowledge base</title><link>https://kbs.yinagi.in/sources/github.com/</link><description>Recent content in Github.com on knowledge base</description><generator>Hugo -- gohugo.io</generator><language>en-us</language><managingEditor>inbox@yinagi.in (murarisumit)</managingEditor><webMaster>inbox@yinagi.in (murarisumit)</webMaster><lastBuildDate>Thu, 04 Aug 2022 15:22:02 +0530</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://kbs.yinagi.in/sources/github.com/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Macos App Switcher</title><link>https://kbs.yinagi.in/en/39e6a85f2560b36262dd276126589bae/</link><pubDate>Thu, 04 Aug 2022 15:22:02 +0530</pubDate><author>inbox@yinagi.in (murarisumit)</author><guid>https://kbs.yinagi.in/en/39e6a85f2560b36262dd276126589bae/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;This is to show macos app switcher in all the monitors connected.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Reset to default state:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;div class="chroma"&gt;
&lt;table class="lntable"&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td class="lntd"&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;1
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class="lntd"&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-fallback" data-lang="fallback"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;defaults delete com.apple.dock; killall Dock
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;then&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;div class="chroma"&gt;
&lt;table class="lntable"&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td class="lntd"&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;1
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;2
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class="lntd"&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-bash" data-lang="bash"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;defaults write com.apple.Dock appswitcher-all-displays -bool &lt;span class="nb"&gt;true&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;killall Dock
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;</description></item><item><title>Rss Reader</title><link>https://kbs.yinagi.in/en/ba2c65ac5f71fbbb97dc75d07ed25f89/</link><pubDate>Sun, 03 Jul 2022 00:47:21 +0530</pubDate><author>inbox@yinagi.in (murarisumit)</author><guid>https://kbs.yinagi.in/en/ba2c65ac5f71fbbb97dc75d07ed25f89/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;Personally I prefer &lt;a href="https://www.reederapp.com"&gt;reederapp&lt;/a&gt;. It has built-in RSS feeds, beautiful interface and sync across devices.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;But if someone is looking for Open Sourcs RSS Reader that works on iOS ecosystem, then &lt;a href="https://netnewswire.com"&gt;netnewswire&lt;/a&gt; is good option without putting lot of money before locking into RSS.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Linuxify</title><link>https://kbs.yinagi.in/en/96b18098f374caabc54fa7d41fdfcecc/</link><pubDate>Mon, 09 May 2022 01:58:48 +0530</pubDate><author>inbox@yinagi.in (murarisumit)</author><guid>https://kbs.yinagi.in/en/96b18098f374caabc54fa7d41fdfcecc/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;Smart scripts to setup the system and eliminating overhead of maintaining scripts.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Bash My Aws</title><link>https://kbs.yinagi.in/en/1b90c167d2d85130fc5372245ed523e9/</link><pubDate>Mon, 09 May 2022 01:42:17 +0530</pubDate><author>inbox@yinagi.in (murarisumit)</author><guid>https://kbs.yinagi.in/en/1b90c167d2d85130fc5372245ed523e9/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;Nice utility to work with awscli faster.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you work with Ip address, ddd this function to bashrc and reload(&lt;code&gt;source ~/.bashrc&lt;/code&gt;) to get instance-id&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;div class="chroma"&gt;
&lt;table class="lntable"&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td class="lntd"&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;1
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;2
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;3
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class="lntd"&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-bash" data-lang="bash"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; get-instance-id&lt;span class="o"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; aws ec2 describe-instances --filters &lt;span class="nv"&gt;Name&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;private-ip-address,Values&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nv"&gt;$1&lt;/span&gt; --query Reservations&lt;span class="o"&gt;[]&lt;/span&gt;.Instances&lt;span class="o"&gt;[]&lt;/span&gt;.InstanceId --output text
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;To get instance id&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;div class="chroma"&gt;
&lt;table class="lntable"&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td class="lntd"&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;1
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class="lntd"&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-bash" data-lang="bash"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;get-instance-id 192.168.1.1
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;To fetch instance tags&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;div class="chroma"&gt;
&lt;table class="lntable"&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td class="lntd"&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;1
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class="lntd"&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-bash" data-lang="bash"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;instance-tags i-0fd5c4df38353cd0
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;</description></item><item><title>Golang Codereview Comments</title><link>https://kbs.yinagi.in/c0ab4091d733d85471515c2cd581fd67/</link><pubDate>Wed, 27 Oct 2021 16:32:43 +0530</pubDate><author>inbox@yinagi.in (murarisumit)</author><guid>https://kbs.yinagi.in/c0ab4091d733d85471515c2cd581fd67/</guid><description/></item><item><title>K8s Failure Stories</title><link>https://kbs.yinagi.in/bookmarks/k8s-failure-stories/</link><pubDate>Mon, 09 Aug 2021 00:37:09 +0530</pubDate><author>inbox@yinagi.in (murarisumit)</author><guid>https://kbs.yinagi.in/bookmarks/k8s-failure-stories/</guid><description/></item><item><title>Awesome Kubernetes</title><link>https://kbs.yinagi.in/bookmarks/awesome-kubernetes/</link><pubDate>Mon, 09 Aug 2021 00:16:59 +0530</pubDate><author>inbox@yinagi.in (murarisumit)</author><guid>https://kbs.yinagi.in/bookmarks/awesome-kubernetes/</guid><description/></item><item><title>Awesome Docker Compose</title><link>https://kbs.yinagi.in/bookmarks/awesome-docker-compose/</link><pubDate>Mon, 09 Aug 2021 00:16:18 +0530</pubDate><author>inbox@yinagi.in (murarisumit)</author><guid>https://kbs.yinagi.in/bookmarks/awesome-docker-compose/</guid><description/></item><item><title>Kuberentes Kbrew</title><link>https://kbs.yinagi.in/bookmarks/k8s-kbrew/</link><pubDate>Sat, 07 Aug 2021 13:33:47 +0530</pubDate><author>inbox@yinagi.in (murarisumit)</author><guid>https://kbs.yinagi.in/bookmarks/k8s-kbrew/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;This tool looks good, and love the ease of this. It&amp;rsquo;s easy way to deploy the applications over cluster.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Awesome K8s Security</title><link>https://kbs.yinagi.in/bookmarks/awesome-k8s-security/</link><pubDate>Sat, 07 Aug 2021 12:50:34 +0530</pubDate><author>inbox@yinagi.in (murarisumit)</author><guid>https://kbs.yinagi.in/bookmarks/awesome-k8s-security/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;A curated list for Kubernetes (K8s) Security resources such as articles, books, tools, talks and videos.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Golang Slice Tricks</title><link>https://kbs.yinagi.in/bookmarks/golang-slice-tricks/</link><pubDate>Wed, 04 Aug 2021 08:29:34 +0530</pubDate><author>inbox@yinagi.in (murarisumit)</author><guid>https://kbs.yinagi.in/bookmarks/golang-slice-tricks/</guid><description>&lt;h3 id="filtering-with-allocating"&gt;Filtering with allocating&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This trick uses the fact that a slice shares the same backing array and capacity as the original, so the storage is reused for the filtered slice. Of course, the original contents are modified.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;div class="chroma"&gt;
&lt;table class="lntable"&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td class="lntd"&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;1
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;2
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;3
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;4
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;5
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;6
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class="lntd"&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-golang" data-lang="golang"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;b&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;:=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;a&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;for&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;_&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;x&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;:=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;range&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;a&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;if&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;f&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;x&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;b&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nb"&gt;append&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;b&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;x&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;</description></item><item><title>Profiles to Look Upto</title><link>https://kbs.yinagi.in/bookmarks/profiles-to-look-upto/</link><pubDate>Fri, 30 Jul 2021 06:35:12 +0530</pubDate><author>inbox@yinagi.in (murarisumit)</author><guid>https://kbs.yinagi.in/bookmarks/profiles-to-look-upto/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;Time to time, few profiles come across to me, which I see and admire of, the amount of work they have done. The position they are in, the impact they are making. Seeing their profiles motivates me.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;These profile answer age old interview question for me: Where do you see youself in 3-5 years ?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;His readme is beautiful, simple and succint. His github is clean. Motivated me also collect those badges(certifications), never a certification guy, but those badges are looking cool.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Azure Caf Terraform Landingzones</title><link>https://kbs.yinagi.in/df6b12d2680b2afbfc3288c0564c3af3/</link><pubDate>Fri, 12 Feb 2021 17:21:31 +0530</pubDate><author>inbox@yinagi.in (murarisumit)</author><guid>https://kbs.yinagi.in/df6b12d2680b2afbfc3288c0564c3af3/</guid><description/></item><item><title>Beautiful Static Site in haskell</title><link>https://kbs.yinagi.in/bookmarks/beautiful-static-site/</link><pubDate>Fri, 12 Jun 2020 14:19:12 +0530</pubDate><author>inbox@yinagi.in (murarisumit)</author><guid>https://kbs.yinagi.in/bookmarks/beautiful-static-site/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;He has made beautiful and optimized site, exactly how work should be like.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Promql cheatsheet</title><link>https://kbs.yinagi.in/bookmarks/promql/</link><pubDate>Wed, 20 May 2020 22:04:04 +0530</pubDate><author>inbox@yinagi.in (murarisumit)</author><guid>https://kbs.yinagi.in/bookmarks/promql/</guid><description/></item></channel></rss>